@essay id="p5-intro" rh="THE 39TH TRIAL · HOW TO USE THIS PART"
# The Trial as story
drop: Volume One treats the Covenant Trials as an institution, how they work in any year. This part is the 39th as a plot. It prints the beats your files already fix, in order, and leaves a chapter column beside each one, so the outline and the files stay in the same place.
The three phases already line up with the novel's three movements. The Temple's phase asks who are you, and the novel calls it Genesis. The Crown's phase asks how smart are you, and it's Exodus. Endurance asks what you're willing to endure, and it's Revelation (TR). Every beat sits under one of the three, and the Trial's own scripture-shaped names are the Empire's choice, which the novel is free to turn.
After the beats come four tools: a tracker of who's still in the Crownward at each phase, the Broadcast's story set against what happened, a map of where each character stands on the book's religious line, and a chapter planner with room for fifty-two chapters.
side:
chips: TR, CR, TL, FR 19–25
k: Content
stext: Two deaths and violence in Endurance. Content notes sit at the top of the pages that carry them.
marg
see: Vol. I, the three phases, {v1:phases}.
/end

