# Before the Crownward
tab:
| Beat | What the files give | Ch. |
| 2101 · the Designation | Highest score in Aurem's history, the flag filed that day. She tells Celeste only when asked, and Celeste goes back to the stove (TL). | _ |
| Bell | Won't sponsor her. Asks about her father and her mother's Binding, and prays a door shut (DR3). | _ |
| The clause and the fee | Six months of paperwork at the kitchen table while Celeste keeps her hands busy. Ten dollars, a red card (TL, DR3). | _ |
| The Regional Assessment | Three days in Aurelia, the board posted at seven in the morning. First (TL, DR3). | _ |
| The Governor-Prelate | Selects her second. His first choice withdraws the night before departure, and it isn't a family health emergency (TR). | _ |
| The household | Solomon prays over her. Zion promises to look after Celeste (TL). | _ |
| The last night | Celeste holds her face and says remember what I told you about the real name of this city (TL). | _ |
prompt: The scene before chapter one that the reader never sees, and what it changes | fill

