# Genesis · weeks one to four
note: A death.
tab:
| Beat | What the files give | Ch. |
| The Settling | The most intense assessment of the four months, presented as a grace period. Everything feeds the score (TR). | _ |
| Sera decides | The first day of the Settling, that afternoon (TR) | _ |
| The Prelate decides | A conclusion about Eden in the first week, shared with no one (CR) | _ |
| The Tea Party | Corinne and Calla's tension begins (TR) | _ |
| The Doctrinal Assessment | Six hours in silence in the Sanctum. Eden's score is the highest in the Trial's history (TR). | _ |
| The Theological Interview | Two hours, three extra pages, and an officer who can't tell aligned from clear-eyed (TR) | _ |
| The Public Testimony | No handler. Lyris, her hands, and Judah, six minutes in. Fourth to first (TR). | _ |
| Petra | Dies before Phase Two. "A sudden medical event." The Trial loses nothing (TR, FR 23–24). | _ |
