@page id="p5-revelation" rh="THE 39TH TRIAL · V · REVELATION, ENDURANCE" m="TKC: TR · MEN · DOM; VOL. I · {v1:mountain}; CONFLICT"
# Revelation · three days in Mountain
note: A killing, a woman left unconscious, and injuries.
tab:
| Beat | What the files give | Ch. |
| Deployment | Filmed. After that, no schedule, no handlers, no cameras. Coordinates to reach across three days. Mountain terrain, for the first time since the 31st Trial, unexplained (TR). | _ |
| Day 1 | Vivienne's ankle fails on a slope, and she's extracted at the first checkpoint. Delphine takes a head injury and is extracted (TR). | _ |
| Day 2 | Corinne pushes Calla into the river. One person sees (TR). | _ |
| Day 3 | Eden and Delphine knock Maren unconscious and leave her (TR). | _ |
| The final checkpoint | Eden, Zara, Sera and Delia. Corinne completes Endurance (TR). | _ |
| The narrative turns | The Broadcast's story about Eden shifts in Phase Three. In Celeste's kitchen, something in Leah goes very still and then very loud (MEN). | _ |
small: CONFLICT: Delphine on Day 1 and Day 3. Five finishers for four places (TR). See Part III.
prompt: What the Broadcast reconstructs of the three days, and what it leaves out | fill

