| Celeste | _ | _ | _ |
| Leah | _ | _ | _ |
| Ruth | _ | _ | _ |
| Nadia | _ | _ | _ |
| Zara | _ | _ | _ |
| Judah | _ | _ | _ |
| Lyris | _ | _ | _ |
| Hannah | _ | _ | _ |
| The Prelate | _ | _ | _ |
| Bell | _ | _ | _ |
small: INTERPRETATION: The faith spreads in each dossier are the evidence. A character who quotes what the Temple reads and hasn't heard what it skips is usually on the usable side.

@page id="p5-book2" rh="THE 39TH TRIAL · X · THREADS INTO BOOK TWO" m="TKC: FR 18 · FR 29 · FR 34 · MEN · TR · CR"
# Threads into book two
rec:
Miriam's father | He knows there are children but not how many or their names, and learned about Eden the day the Trial went public. He's the only person watching who understands what he's looking at (FR 18).
The 2085 cohort | Twelve women who know each other from being measured against each other, scattered through their Dominions. A network that doesn't wake before book two (FR 34).
Solomon | The teacher notes Eden doesn't know about, and the moment she understands winning was a beginning (MEN).
Naomi | Entered or taken out, depending on what Eden's win proves (FR 29).
Delia | What she does as a Lady in Waiting (TR).
Sera | A flag updated after the Trial, privately (TR).
The Registry | Whoever controls what it says controls something more basic than law. Eden will understand this before most people do (CR).
The Dissent | Wherever Dorian keeps it (FR 42).
prompt: The thread I'm adding | fill
